{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.QHookVandermonde","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QHookVandermonde","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBetaGapVandermonde"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.prodHooksF_one_sub_pow_vandermonde","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.prodHooksF_one_sub_pow_vandermonde","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QHookVandermonde.lean#L86-L106","doc":"**The q-hook product against a genuine Vandermonde (divisor-free).**\n\n`∏_c (1 − Q^{h_λ(c)}) · ∏_{i<j} (x_i − x_j) = (∏_{i<j} (−x_j)) · ∏_i ∏_{m=1}^{β_i} (1 − Q^m)`,\nat `x_i = Q^{β_i}`.\n\nThis is `prodHooksF_one_sub_pow_pair` in the node coordinates the `LagrangeCoeffSum` family uses.\nThe monomial-and-sign factor `∏_{i<j}(−x_j)` sits on the right rather than being evaluated; it is\nthe same factor on both sides of any ratio of two such products, so it cancels wherever this is\nconsumed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.vandermonde_pair_prod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.vandermonde_pair_prod","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QHookVandermonde.lean#L69-L84","doc":"**The Vandermonde pair product, in terms of the `(1 − Q^…)` pair product.**\n\n`∏_{i<j} (x_i − x_j) = (∏_{i<j} (−x_j)) · ∏_{i<j} (1 − Q^{β_i − β_j})`, at `x_i = Q^{β_i}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.qPow_betaNum_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.qPow_betaNum_sub","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QHookVandermonde.lean#L50-L67","doc":"**The termwise conversion.** `x_i − x_j = (−x_j)·(1 − Q^{β_i − β_j})` at `x_i = Q^{β_i}`.\n\nThis is where the `ℕ`-subtraction is discharged: `β_j ≤ β_i` lets `Q^{β_i}` split as\n`Q^{β_j} · Q^{β_i − β_j}`, and the rest is `ring`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.betaNum_lt_betaNum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTBeta.betaNum_lt_betaNum","kind":"theorem","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QHookVandermonde.lean#L41-L48","doc":"**`β` is strictly decreasing.** On a weakly-decreasing shape the parts are antitone and the\n`(length − 1 − i)` staircase is strictly antitone, so their sum is strictly antitone. ","signatureChunk":0}]}